      {
        tag: "table",
        id: "sandalsSeedReqs",
        columns: "seed:string|charge:number",
        children: [
          // `SandalsOfNature.seedChargeReqs` (tag `v3.3.8`), keyed by this port's own plant-kind
          // spelling (`seedPlantKind()`'s normalized class name) rather than Java's
          // `Class<? extends Plant.Seed>` - the port's seeds are one generic `'seed'` id carrying a
          // `sourceClass`, so the concrete class name is what survives. One role here: the
          // `AC_ROOT` charge gate. Java also hands the same number to `Artifact.artifactProc` on a
          // successful root, but runs three talent-driven effects and nothing else at `v3.3.8` - the Priest subclass detonates an Illuminated target for `5 + hero.lvl`, the Cleric's SearingLight marks it, and the Huntress's Sunray rolls `1 + 2*points`/20 for Blindness - so its own `artifLevel`/`chargesUsed` parameters are read by nothing. This port has none of those three talents (no `GuidingLight`/`SearingLight`/`Sunray`), which is why it does not call it - so
          // the gate is the only real consumer of these values in this port.
          { tag: "row", seed: "rotberry", charge: 8 },
          { tag: "row", seed: "firebloom", charge: 20 },
          { tag: "row", seed: "swiftthistle", charge: 20 },
